    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d813">

                <pb facs="1496" n="1462" sameAs="frus:frus1948v02/pg1462"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Council/2–1448: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in the United Kingdom
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-02-14T12:00:00-05:00">February 14,
                            1948—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>502. For USDel. Following suggested to
                    representatives Brit and French Embs here as subjects US believes desirable to
                    consider in tripartite discussions on German assets question prior to initial
                    session Deputies for Austria: <pb facs="1497" n="1463" xml:id="pg1463"/>
                    <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Whether Brit and French are prepared to go ahead with French proposal
                            as basis of settlement with Soviets on German assets question?</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>If it appears final settlement can be reached, what are maximum
                            percentage concessions which Brit and French would make in effecting
                            compromise falling somewhere between French proposal and Soviet proposal
                            with reference to: (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) oil production; (<hi
                                rendition="#italic">b</hi>) oil exploration rights; (<hi
                                rendition="#italic">c</hi>) refining capacity, and (<hi
                                rendition="#italic">d</hi>) DDSG?</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Qualifications concerning oil to ensure largest measure Austrian
                            sovereignty and to limit Soviet economic influence in Austria: (<hi
                                rendition="#italic">a</hi>) duration of concessions for exploration
                            and production; (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) extent of immunity from
                            nationalization of Soviet oil properties; (<hi rendition="#italic"
                                >c</hi>) conditions under which Soviet Union may remove exportable
                            production with provision for satisfaction of Austria’s domestic
                            requirements.</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>Redemption obligations: (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) maximum
                            amount; (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) period over which redemption
                            can be spread; (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) optional arrangements as
                            to form of payment, including payments in currency, in kind, and in
                            value added to non-indigenous raw materials; (<hi rendition="#italic"
                                >d</hi>) initial moratorium period.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
